# Blue/green ingress for NomNomzBot (deployment-distribution.md, slice Z5). Caddy owns the
# documented API port (docker-compose.yml maps ${API_HTTP_PORT:-5080} to this container's :80)
# and load-balances across BOTH api-blue and api-green — chosen because open-source Caddy
# supports ACTIVE upstream health checks out of the box (polling /health/ready on an interval,
# not just reacting to failed proxied requests), which open-source nginx does not; Caddy is also
# a single static binary with no extra module build, keeping the ingress layer as few moving
# parts as possible.
#
# `health_status 200` means an upstream failing /health/ready (503 while draining or not-yet-
# ready) is excluded from the pool immediately — scripts/switchover.ps1 relies on exactly this so
# it never has to touch this file or reload Caddy: starting the idle colour and stopping the old
# one is enough, because Caddy's own health poller notices both transitions on its own.

:80 {
	reverse_proxy api-blue:5000 api-green:5000 {
		lb_policy first
		health_uri /health/ready
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 3s
		health_status 200
	}
}
